@inject Microsoft.Extensions.Options.IOptions<RestaurantMenu.Services.BrandOptions> BrandSettings
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Terms of use";
    var brand = BrandSettings.Value;
}

<article class="prose">
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="lead">The rules for restaurants using My Quick Menu, and for guests using a restaurant's menu, ordering and bookings.</p>
    <p><small>Last updated 23 November 2026.</small></p>

    <h2 id="service">1. The service</h2>
    <p>My Quick Menu ("we") is built and operated by <strong>@brand.LegalEntity</strong>@(string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(brand.LegalNipt) ? "" : $" (NIPT {brand.LegalNipt.Trim()})"), Albania (<a href="@brand.ParentUrl" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">@(new Uri(brand.ParentUrl).Host)</a>). It gives restaurants digital menus, table ordering, a kitchen display, table bookings, a restaurant website, guest feedback and back-office tools for stock, shifts and sales. How we handle personal data is described in the <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Privacy">Privacy</a> page, which is part of these terms.</p>

    <h2 id="restaurants">2. For restaurants</h2>
    <h3>Accounts</h3>
    <p>You can sign up on our website (we may check a new account before it opens), or we set the account up for you and send an invite link. Owners can invite their own team. You are responsible for everything done under your account and your team's accounts, for keeping passwords private, and for removing people who no longer work with you.</p>

    <h3>Your content</h3>
    <p>You are responsible for everything you publish: dish names, descriptions, photos, prices, opening hours, and in particular <strong>allergen and dietary information</strong>. We show what you enter; we don't check it. Keep it accurate and up to date, as the law requires of food businesses.</p>
    <p>You keep all rights to your content. You allow us to store, display and adapt it (for example resize photos or produce translations you ask for) only to provide the service. Only upload content you have the right to use.</p>

    <h3>Your guests</h3>
    <p>Orders, bookings and ratings are between you and your guests. You decide whether to accept them, you serve and charge for orders, and you honour bookings. You must use guests' details only to serve them, and handle them as data protection law requires.</p>

    <h3 id="plans">Plans, prices and payment</h3>
    <p>A subscription is made of the modules and the number of branches you choose. Prices are shown on the <a href="/pricing">Pricing</a> page in euros, without VAT, which is added where it applies. Subscriptions are billed <strong>monthly or yearly in advance</strong> and <strong>renew automatically</strong> at the end of each period until you cancel. New accounts can try the service free for 14 days, without a card.</p>
    <p>You can pay by card or by bank transfer. <strong>Card payments:</strong> our order process is conducted by our online reseller <strong>Paddle.com</strong>. Paddle.com is the Merchant of Record for all our card orders; Paddle provides customer service for those payments and handles returns, and its <a href="https://www.paddle.com/legal/checkout-buyer-terms" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">buyer terms</a> apply to them. <strong>Bank transfer:</strong> we send you an invoice, payable by the due date shown on it.</p>
    <p>If a payment fails or an invoice isn't paid, your account gets 14 days' grace. After that the back office becomes read-only and paid features pause until the payment is made; your data is kept and your public menus stay online. We announce price changes at least 30 days in advance by email; they apply from your next renewal.</p>

    <h3 id="cancel">Cancelling and refunds</h3>
    <p>You can cancel at any time on the Billing page of your account, or by emailing us. Cancelling stops the next renewal; you keep access until the end of the period you have paid for. You can get a <strong>full refund of your first payment within 14 days</strong>; renewals are not refunded except where the law requires it. Details are in our <a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="Refunds">Refund policy</a>, which is part of these terms.</p>
    <p>You can also ask us to erase your account and data. We may suspend or close an account that breaks these terms, puts others at risk or remains unpaid, after warning you where reasonably possible.</p>

    <h2 id="guests">3. For guests</h2>
    <p>Menus, prices and availability are published by each restaurant, which is responsible for them. If you have an allergy or intolerance, always confirm with the staff before ordering.</p>
    <p>Sending an order from your table or booking a table is an arrangement with the restaurant, not with us. Payment is made to the restaurant as it tells you. Please cancel bookings you can't keep, using the link you received.</p>
    <p>Don't send fake orders, bookings or ratings, and don't try to disrupt the service.</p>

    <h2 id="use">4. Fair use</h2>
    <p>Nobody may use My Quick Menu to publish illegal, misleading or offensive content, to send spam, to access accounts or data that aren't theirs, or to overload or probe the service.</p>

    <h2 id="availability">5. Availability and changes</h2>
    <p>We work to keep the service available and your data safe, with backups, but we can't promise it will never be interrupted. We may improve or change features; if a change takes away something you rely on, we tell you in advance.</p>

    <h2 id="liability">6. Liability</h2>
    <p>We are not responsible for the content restaurants publish, or for what happens between a restaurant and its guests. As far as the law allows, our liability to a restaurant is limited to the fees it paid us in the 12 months before the claim. Nothing in these terms limits liability that the law does not allow to be limited.</p>

    <h2 id="law">7. Law and changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Albania. If we change them, we update the date above and tell restaurants of important changes in advance.</p>

    <h2 id="contact">8. Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about these terms, billing or refunds: <a href="mailto:@brand.Email">@brand.Email</a>, or <a href="/contact">other ways to reach us</a>.</p>
</article>
